# The three above re-ran the formatter after a configuration change, so each
# rewrote most of the tree without altering a line of code. They also carry the
# .clang-format change that caused the rewrite; blame ignores a commit wholesale
# rather than per file, so blame on .clang-format itself will skip past them to
# the commit that introduced the file. That is the right trade: the sources are
# what anyone actually blames.
#
# The merge commit is deliberately absent -- git cannot ignore a merge, and the
# lines it touched were rewritten again by the commits above in any case.
